section": "mdna", "score": 0.5087, "filing_name": "Target Corporation 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/27419/000002741925000018/tgt-20250201.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "TGT_10K_2025-02-01__business__0024", "ticker": "TGT", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-02-01", "section": "business", "score": 0.722, "filing_name": "Target Corporation 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/27419/000002741925000018/tgt-20250201.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "TGT_10K_2025-02-01__business__0017", "ticker": "TGT", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-02-01", "section": "business", "score": 0.5905, "filing_name": "Target Corporation 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/27419/000002741925000018/tgt-20250201.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "TGT_10K_2025-02-01__business__0000", "ticker": "TGT", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-02-01", "section": "business", "score": 0.5121, "filing_name": "Target Corporation 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/27419/000002741925000018/tgt-20250201.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 15, "dropped_candidates": 39, "token_estimate": 28521, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "Target's 10-K for fiscal 2025 (period ended February 1, 2025) groups its risks under competitive and reputational, supply chain and third-party, information security, investment and infrastructure, legal and regulatory, and financial headings. The filing does not rank them, so none is flagged as most severe. Competitive and reputational risks include failing to differentiate from competitors [TGT_10K_2025-02-01__risk_factors__0000] and negative perceptions tied to environmental, social, and governance expectations [TGT_10K_2025-02-01__risk_factors__0005]. Supply chain risks include tariffs, with China the largest source of imported merchandise [TGT_10K_2025-02-01__risk_factors__0020], and cybersecurity incidents could disrupt operations [TGT_10K_2025-02-01__risk_factors__0017]. Target also cites dependence on U.S. macroeconomic conditions and consumer spending [TGT_10K_2025-02-01__risk_factors__0024].", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "TGT", "company": "Target Corporation", "findings": [{"point": "Competitive risk: if Target cannot differentiate its guest experience from competitors, results of operations and financial condition could be adversely affected.", "citations": ["TGT_10K_2025-02-01__risk_factors__0000"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Reputational risk: Target says it has been unable to meet conflicting stakeholder expectations on environmental, social, and governance matters, which led to negative publicity, consumer boycotts, and litigation.", "citations": ["TGT_10K_2025-02-01__risk_factors__0005"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Supply chain and trade risk: China is the single largest source of imported merchandise, and additional tariffs or duties could require price increases or alternative sourcing.", "citations": ["TGT_10K_2025-02-01__risk_factors__0020"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Information security risk: additional significant incidents could severely disrupt operations and expose Target to enforcement actions and litigation, and Target previously experienced a prominent data breach.", "citations": ["TGT_10K_2025-02-01__risk_factors__0017"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Macroeconomic risk: nearly all sales are in the U.S., so results are highly dependent on the U.S. economy and consumer confidence and spending.", "citations": ["TGT_10K_2025-02-01__risk_factors__0024"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Inventory risk: elevated inventory shrink, including theft from organized retail crime, has adversely affected results and contributed to store closures and long-term asset impairments.", "citations": ["TGT_10K_2025-02-01__risk_factors__0009", "